Changes relative to the original (summary; the full account is in docs/PORTING_NOTES.md):
  * Ported from RimWorld 1.4 to RimWorld 1.6 (changed vanilla signatures, pathfinding API, storage search).
  * Harmony IL transpilers replaced by semantic prefix/postfix/finalizer hooks with failure-safe gating.
  * Detour bookkeeping rewritten around explicit per-pawn plans with a defined lifecycle.
  * Pick Up And Haul integration ("PUAH+") is NOT part of this baseline; see README.
  * The CodeOptimist library is not merged as a separate DLL; only the parts actually needed are carried.
  * New package id and new identity: this is a separate project. The original Steam Workshop
    PublishedFileId is deliberately not reused.

Not part of this repository
---------------------------
  * RimWorld / Ludeon Studios assemblies and content. Compile against your own installation
    (-p:RimWorldManagedDir=...) or the Krafs.Rimworld.Ref reference-assembly NuGet package.
  * Harmony (Andreas Pardeike, MIT) is required at runtime via the Harmony mod (brrainz.harmony) and
    referenced at build time through the Lib.Harmony NuGet package (compile-only).
  * Krafs.Publicizer (Krafs, MIT) is used at build time only.
